 },
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Tuples of morphisms with one immersion",
 "statement": "Let $S$ be a scheme, let $Y_1,\\dots,Y_m$ be schemes over $S$ and let\n$f_i\\colon T\\to Y_i$ be morphisms of $S$-schemes. If some $f_k$ is an\nimmersion, then\n\n$$\n(f_1,\\dots,f_m)\\colon T\\longrightarrow Y_1\\times_S\\dots\\times_S Y_m\n$$\n\nis an immersion.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-proper-base-change/sk-thm-chow/lem-chow-tuple-immersion.md",
  "place": "node lem-chow-tuple-immersion, order 1055"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Composing $(f_1,\\dots,f_m)$ with the projection $\\mathrm{pr}_k$ gives back\n$f_k$, which is an immersion; hence $(f_1,\\dots,f_m)$ is an immersion, because\nif a composition $h\\circ g$ is an immersion then so is $g$.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  },
  {
   "text": "(The blueprint originally deduced this from 01KR by factoring\n$(f_1,\\dots,f_m)$ through $T\\times_S Y_2\\times_S\\dots\\times_S Y_m$, which also\nrequires the $Y_i$ to be separated over $S$. The argument above needs neither.)",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  }
 ],
